#
# Competency cells for the pipeline slice — the runtime-DAG vocabulary.
#
# The central conformance claim of the vocabulary is executable here: an AUTHORITY
# edge is a first-class ordering constraint that survives admission even though no
# bytes flow across it. The cell pins the exact edge BY IRI, so a data change that
# retyped the authority edge as a plain dataflow edge (the exact reduction a pure-
# dataflow reasoner performs) drops the pinned row and fails, and a change that
# silently added a second authority edge also fails — closed-set drift in both
# directions, which is what the question exists to catch.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/pipeline/tests/> .
@prefix exd:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/pipeline/> .

ex:cqAuthorityEdgeRetained a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/pipeline/queries/competency/cq-authority-edge-retained.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqDataFile "examples/in-rush-enrichment-dag.ttl" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The in-rush enrichment DAG ships one authority edge, exd:edge-gate-authority, from the admission gate to the receipt writer. No bytes flow across it — the writer reads its data from ex:enrich through a plain gmeow:dataflowConsumes edge — so a reasoner that reduced the DAG to its byte-flow skeleton would find no dependency between the gate and the writer and drop the ordering, letting a receipt be written before the admission verdict exists. That is precisely the corruption gmeow:RuntimeDagAdmissionConstraint (d) forbids and gmeow:flowReasonAuthority exists to prevent. Pinning the authority edge BY IRI rather than by a bare count is what makes the question probative: a count of one survives a retype that quietly turns the authority edge into a gmeow:flowReasonDataflow edge and adds an unrelated authority edge elsewhere, and that retype is the drift a pure-dataflow reduction performs. The single expected row is the admission law's promise made executable — the authority ordering is kept, not dropped."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqAuthorityEdgeRetainedShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqAuthorityEdgeRow .

ex:cqAuthorityEdgeRetainedShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "edge" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsExact .

ex:cqAuthorityEdgeRow a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "edge" ; gmeow:cellValueIri exd:edge-gate-authority ] .

# The cache policy is authored as a closed semantic contract, not inferred from
# timings. This cell pins its class/property range and the production verifier's
# persistent-contribution declaration in one exact row.
ex:cqCacheDispositionContract a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion ;
    gmeow:cqQueryFile "slices/core/pipeline/queries/competency/cache-disposition-contract.rq" ;
    gmeow:cqReasoning gmeow:reasoningNone ;
    gmeow:cqRationale "The scheduler may persist only an independently bounded stage contribution, while a cumulative carrier must be reconstructed from the live frontier. This question binds the closed gmeow:StageCacheDisposition value class to its gmeow:stageCacheDisposition property and to the production gmeow:stage-verify-attestation declaration. If any of those three links drifts, the executable and authored DAG can disagree about what is safe to hydrate, allowing an aggregate snapshot or an unverified output to masquerade as the exact bounded contribution."@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:cqResultShape ex:cqCacheDispositionContractShape ;
    gmeow:cqExactRows true ;
    gmeow:cqExpectRow ex:cqCacheDispositionContractRow .

ex:cqCacheDispositionContractShape a logic:ResultShape ;
    logic:declaresColumn
        [ logic:columnVariable "valueClass" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "property" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ,
        [ logic:columnVariable "stage" ; logic:columnTermKind logic:TermKindIri ; logic:columnBinding logic:BindingRequired ] ;
    logic:shapeCardinality logic:RowsExact .

ex:cqCacheDispositionContractRow a gmeow:ExpectedRow ;
    gmeow:rowCell
        [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "valueClass" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:StageCacheDisposition ] ,
        [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "property" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:stageCacheDisposition ] ,
        [ a gmeow:ExpectedCell ; gmeow:cellVar "stage" ; gmeow:cellValueIri gmeow:stage-verify-attestation ] .
